Z||000000||KRMFiero||09-26-2000||04:31 PM||||I have a 1984 Fiero SE 2M4, gray interier anyways, my seats are ripped up and stuff and i dont want to reapulster them, i'm not good with that stuff. Where can I find new seats with the speakers built in, or a place i can send the seats out to re do all the material on the outside. (also if there is a place that does that when the seats are apart could they change the speakers to? if so what size are the speakers?) <P>Thank you<P>Kyle  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||09-26-2000||05:47 PM||||<BR>KRM, first welcome to the forum.<P>Second regarding the seats, Mr. Mikes leather is a excellent method of recovering your seats.  And from what I have read, he provides an instructional video that helps you do the work yourself.<P>The material is not real cheap, but compared to some cloth products it is relatively similiar and provides better wear.<P>Here is Mr Mikes website: <A HREF="http://www.mrmikes.com" TARGET=_blank>www.mrmikes.com</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.txconnect.com/home/rharris/signature-a.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||09-26-2000||07:27 PM||||The speakers are 3.5" round.  Crutchfield has 2 or 3 different ones.||||reg||1
Z||000003||KRMFiero||09-26-2000||07:42 PM||||Thank you for your information, but are those seat covers or does it replace the fabric?<P><BR>thanx||||reg||1
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||09-26-2000||07:57 PM||||KRM, we can call them seat skins. They replace the old fabric. You are not putting on seat covers, you are re-doing the seats??<P>See:www.mrmikes.com<BR>Also see: more gray and more gray topic<BR>And welcome to the spot!!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>DXR_DAD||||reg||3
Z||000005||KRMFiero||09-26-2000||08:59 PM||||Thank you that is what i kind of thought but i was not sure.   when i take the skin off how hard will it be to change the speaker? thank you Kyle<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||TOM||09-27-2000||01:44 AM||||I have one seta back and one bottom for an 84SE grey. Make an offer. It is in real nice condition.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Carrolles||09-27-2000||04:44 PM||||With the skin removed the speaker just pulls out of the hole in the foam padding.  It is not bolted in.<P>BTW speakers can be added to 86 thru 88 seats using Mr. Mikes procedure.  There is a write-up with lots of pictures and diagrams on his site.||||reg||1
